{"name":"Speckled Easter Egg","hex":"#d38798","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"speckled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Marked with dots or spots, spotted.","Sporadically and irregularly marked."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speckled"},{"term":"easter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Eastern. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","comparative form of east: more east"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An easterly wind (a wind blowing from the east); especially, a strong one; a storm of such winds."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/easter"},{"term":"egg","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food.","An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something).","To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egg"}],"entries":[{"title":"Easter egg","blocks":[{"text":"Easter eggs, also called Paschal eggs, are eggs that are decorated for the Christian festival of Easter, which celebrates the resurrection of Jesus. As such, Easter eggs are commonly used during the season of Eastertide. The oldest tradition, which continues to be used in Central and Eastern Europe, is to dye and paint chicken eggs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Bg-easter-eggs.jpg/330px-Bg-easter-eggs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Easter_egg","wikidata":"Q163886"},{"title":"Easter","blocks":[{"text":"Easter, also called Pasch or Pascha or Resurrection Sunday, is a Christian celebration and cultural holiday commemorating the resurrection of Jesus from the dead, described in the Bible's New Testament as having occurred on the third day of his burial following his crucifixion by the Romans at Calvary c. 30 AD. It is the culmination of the Passion of Jesus, preceded by Lent, a 40-day period of fasting, prayer, and penance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Chora_Anastasis2.jpg/330px-Chora_Anastasis2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Easter","wikidata":"Q21196"},{"title":"Egg","blocks":[{"text":"An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has developed enough to survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg/330px-Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg","wikidata":"Q17147"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Unfinished_pysanka.jpg/500px-Unfinished_pysanka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Unfinished_pysanka.jpg/500px-Unfinished_pysanka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Easter egg of the Ukrainian variety with the Paschal greeting \"Christ is Risen!\" ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUnfinished_pysanka.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Osterei_Verzierung%2C_March_2010.jpg/500px-Osterei_Verzierung%2C_March_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Osterei_Verzierung%2C_March_2010.jpg/500px-Osterei_Verzierung%2C_March_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A chocolate Easter egg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOsterei_Verzierung%2C_March_2010.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Hungarian_easter_eggs_06.jpg/500px-Hungarian_easter_eggs_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Hungarian_easter_eggs_06.jpg/1280px-Hungarian_easter_eggs_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Hungarian_easter_eggs_06.jpg/500px-Hungarian_easter_eggs_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Easter eggs of Hungary, called hímestojás are handmade and gifted during Locsolkodás typically as courting or to family. It is also used in ticselés which is traditional gambling for kids.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHungarian_easter_eggs_06.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Red_Paschal_Egg_with_Cross.JPG/500px-Red_Paschal_Egg_with_Cross.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Red_Paschal_Egg_with_Cross.JPG/